      "value": "@{5ce09c4ff1ef661188867ab5|full_name}: If by \"Python\" you mean \"Photon\", that's only partly the cause of the problem. The Photon servers are currently the only thing that don't support IPv6 but that shouldn't be a problem for almost all users since every ISP at least does IPv4 NAT for fallback connectivity if a service doesn't have IPv6. The client not receiving invite requests or being able to send invites, refresh the friends list, etc. is a different problem that's caused by the authcookie being locked to a single IP address and that entire thing just falls apart when the client sends a HTTP/Websocket request from an IP address that the API servers aren't expecting.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
